<h1>Decisioning Platform — UI Architecture</h1>
<p class="meta">Updated August 30, 2026 · React + TypeScript UI · Industry design system (indigo #4a5ac9, local-only fonts) · §13 capability module structure · §14 browser memory and component interaction</p>

<h2>1. Purpose and scope</h2>
<p>This document describes the UI architecture of the Decisioning Platform and how to consume the Industry design system in a React codebase. It covers the approved scope only: SSO login, the authenticated shell, Home, Workflows (inventory + BPMN detail), Graph view, Rules (inventory + detail), Executions (inventory + trace), and visible-but-deferred Monitoring, Documentation and Examples. Workflow authoring, Intent, Decisions, Data, Connectors, Scripts, Tasks and Alerts are hidden, not disabled (FR-SHELL-010). Backend APIs, transport and persistence are out of scope; the UI runs on dummy-data adapters that do not constrain future contracts (FR-MOCK-003).</p>

<h2>2. How to use the design system in your React code</h2>
<h3>Step 1 — Adopt the token stylesheet</h3>
<p>Copy <code>styles.css</code> into your app as the global stylesheet. It is the single source of truth: color roles with 100–900 tonal ramps, fixed semantic status colors, spacing, radius, elevation, shell layout dimensions, and font stacks. <b>Fonts are local-only</b> — every named family ships with the operating system; nothing downloads (ADR-019). Never hard-code a hex or px value the tokens carry; theme and accent changes happen by remapping tokens, never per-page overrides (NFR-REACT-005).</p>
<h3>Step 2 — Port the component primitives</h3>
<p>Each component under <code>components/platform-*/</code> is a pair: <code>&lt;Name&gt;.jsx</code> (reference implementation) and <code>&lt;Name&gt;.d.ts</code> (typed prop contract, annotated with the requirement/ADR it satisfies). Port them 1:1 into your component library; convert to TypeScript by merging the <code>.d.ts</code> props into the function signature. Components style themselves from <code>var(--*)</code> tokens and the system classes (<code>.btn</code>, <code>.table</code>, <code>.input</code>, <code>.seg</code>, <code>.blueprint</code>), so they re-theme automatically.</p>
<h3>Step 3 — Or start from the ready-made TypeScript project</h3>
<p><code>templates/react-ts-handoff/</code> is a standalone Vite + React + TypeScript project with all of this already done: the 14 primitives as typed <code>.tsx</code> (each merges its <code>.d.ts</code> interface with the implementation; cross-references are real imports, no globals), every approved page, fixtures, and the token sheet. <code>npm install &amp;&amp; npm run dev</code>. It ships <code>strict: false</code> to stay 1:1 with the reference implementation — enable strict and annotate incrementally.</p>
<h3>Step 4 — Compose pages from the primitives</h3>
<p><code>templates/platform-app/</code> is the working interactive application: <code>app.jsx</code> (shell wiring + navigation), <code>pages-build.jsx</code> and <code>pages-monitor.jsx</code> (page components for every approved screen), <code>fixtures.js</code> (dummy data). To productionize:</p>
<ul>
<li>Replace the internal state router in <code>app.jsx</code> with React Router routes (table in §4) and lazy-load the page modules (<code>React.lazy</code>) per NFR-REACT-006.</li>
<li>Replace <code>fixtures.js</code> with data adapters behind hooks (e.g. <code>useWorkflows(tenant)</code>); keep pages unaware of transport.</li>
<li>Wire <code>onNavigate</code>/<code>onRowClick</code>/<code>go()</code> callbacks to router navigation, and the tenant selector to your context provider (tenant change rescopes all queries and search, FR-SHELL-005).</li>
</ul>
<div class="callout"><b>Rule of thumb:</b> pages compose primitives and tokens; they never define colors, fonts or status treatments of their own (NFR-REACT-004).</div>

<h2>3. Layered architecture</h2>
<p>Each layer depends only on the layers below it:</p>
<table style="width:100%;margin:6pt 0 10pt">
<tr><td style="background:#eef0fb;border:1.5pt solid #4a5ac9;text-align:center;padding:7pt"><b>1 · Identity boundary</b><br><span class="mono">LoginPage · UserContextProvider (roles, permissions, tenants)</span></td></tr>
<tr><td style="border:none;text-align:center;padding:1pt;color:#4a5ac9">▼</td></tr>
<tr><td style="background:#eef0fb;border:1.5pt solid #4a5ac9;text-align:center;padding:7pt"><b>2 · Persistent shell</b><br><span class="mono">AppShell = Sidebar + TopBar (Tenant · Search · Profile) + Breadcrumbs</span></td></tr>
<tr><td style="border:none;text-align:center;padding:1pt;color:#4a5ac9">▼</td></tr>
<tr><td style="background:#f5f5f8;border:1pt solid #9aa2d6;text-align:center;padding:7pt"><b>3 · Route modules (lazy)</b><br><span class="mono">Home · Workflows · WorkflowDetail · Graph · Rules · RuleDetail · Executions · Trace</span></td></tr>
<tr><td style="border:none;text-align:center;padding:1pt;color:#4a5ac9">▼</td></tr>
<tr><td style="background:#f5f5f8;border:1pt solid #9aa2d6;text-align:center;padding:7pt"><b>4 · Shared primitives</b><br><span class="mono">MetricCard · DataTable · StatusIndicator · Canvas · WorkflowNode · Edge · NodeInspector …</span></td></tr>
<tr><td style="border:none;text-align:center;padding:1pt;color:#4a5ac9">▼</td></tr>
<tr><td style="background:#fff;border:1pt solid #d4d4d7;text-align:center;padding:7pt"><b>5 · Tokens &amp; theming</b><br><span class="mono">styles.css custom properties — remapped on :root, never overridden per page</span></td></tr>
<tr><td style="border:none;text-align:center;padding:1pt;color:#4a5ac9">▼</td></tr>
<tr><td style="background:#fff;border:1pt solid #d4d4d7;text-align:center;padding:7pt"><b>6 · Data boundary</b><br><span class="mono">Dummy-data adapters · tenant-scoped queries · no secrets in the UI</span></td></tr>
</table>
<table>
<tr><th>Layer</th><th>Contents</th><th>Key decisions</th></tr>
<tr><td><b>1 · Identity boundary</b></td><td>LoginPage, UserContextProvider (identity, roles, permissions, tenants, environments)</td><td>SSO only; no persona/tenant picker at login; UI shows only permitted resources (ADR-001/002)</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>2 · Persistent shell</b></td><td>AppShell, Sidebar, TopBar (TenantToggle · GlobalSearch · ProfileMenu), Breadcrumbs</td><td>Same shell for all authenticated views; profile menu is appearance-only: theme System/Light/Dark + accent Indigo/Blue/Teal/Purple (ADR-003/005/006)</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>3 · Route modules (lazy)</b></td><td>Home, Workflows, WorkflowDetail, Graph, Rules, RuleDetail, Executions, Trace</td><td>List/detail on separate routes; inventory never shows the BPMN beside the list (ADR-007/014/015)</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>4 · Shared primitives</b></td><td>Component inventory (§5)</td><td>Typed props for variant, status, size, state (NFR-REACT-002)</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>5 · Tokens &amp; theming</b></td><td>CSS custom properties + typed tokens</td><td>Accent is user-selectable; semantic status colors are fixed across all themes (ADR-006/018)</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>6 · Data boundary</b></td><td>Dummy-data adapters, tenant-scoped queries</td><td>Mock shapes do not define API contracts (FR-MOCK-003); secrets never reach the UI (NFR-SEC-003)</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>4. Routes</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>Route</th><th>Page</th><th>Notes</th></tr>
<tr><td class="mono">/login</td><td>SSO login</td><td>Work email + Continue with SSO only</td></tr>
<tr><td class="mono">/home</td><td>Home dashboard</td><td>Welcome, 4 metrics, My Workflows, Recent Executions, Announcements, Usage chart</td></tr>
<tr><td class="mono">/workflows</td><td>Workflows inventory</td><td>Tenant metrics, + Workflow (permission-gated), search/filter, infinite scroll</td></tr>
<tr><td class="mono">/workflows/{workflowId}</td><td>BPMN view</td><td>Status/Version/Executions/Avg-duration metrics, vertical BPMN canvas + node inspector</td></tr>
<tr><td class="mono">/workflows/{workflowId}/graphs/{graphId}</td><td>Graph (DAG) view</td><td>No workflow metric cards; zoom/fit/center/validate; breadcrumbs preserve workflow context</td></tr>
<tr><td class="mono">/rules · /rules/{ruleId}</td><td>Rules inventory / detail</td><td>Detail: definition (monospace) main pane, properties right pane</td></tr>
<tr><td class="mono">/executions</td><td>Executions inventory</td><td>Default: last 7 days, start-date descending; filters reset scroll position</td></tr>
</table>

