<p style="font-size:9pt;color:#5d5d60">Home, Rules and Executions are reached from the sidebar at any time; breadcrumbs walk detail pages back to their inventories.</p>

<h2>5. Component inventory</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>Component</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Key props</th><th>Satisfies</th></tr>
<tr><td><b>AppShell</b></td><td>Sidebar + TopBar + breadcrumbs around scrolling content; owns sidebar collapse</td><td class="mono">nav, topBar, breadcrumbs, children</td><td>ADR-003</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>Sidebar</b></td><td>Capability navigation (Build/Monitor/Learn) with collapse; active item indigo-on-tint</td><td class="mono">sections, activeId, collapsed, onNavigate</td><td>FR-SHELL-008/009, ADR-018</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>TopBar</b></td><td>Tenant label/selector, scoped global search, profile card with appearance menu</td><td class="mono">tenant, tenants, user, onSearch, theme, accent</td><td>FR-SHELL-002/003/004, ADR-006</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>Breadcrumbs</b></td><td>Clickable trail; last crumb is current page, not clickable</td><td class="mono">items[{label, onClick}]</td><td>ADR-013</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>PageHeader</b></td><td>Title + subtitle + right-aligned action slot</td><td class="mono">title, subtitle, actions</td><td>—</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>MetricCard</b></td><td>KPI tile: kicker, large value, caption, trend</td><td class="mono">label, value, caption, trend</td><td>FR-WF-002, FR-RULE-001</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>StatusIndicator</b></td><td>Fixed status language; always dot/glyph + text, never color alone</td><td class="mono">status, variant ('badge'|'text'), label</td><td>ADR-018, NFR-A11Y-003</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>TrendIndicator</b></td><td>Arrow direction decoupled from semantic color (business effect)</td><td class="mono">direction, tone, label</td><td>ADR-018</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>Badge</b></td><td>Tinted label; mono variant for IDs and versions</td><td class="mono">tone, mono, children</td><td>—</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>DataTable</b></td><td>Themed table; React-node cells; keyboard-operable clickable rows</td><td class="mono">columns, rows, rowKey, onRowClick, empty</td><td>NFR-A11Y-002/005</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>Canvas</b></td><td>Scrollable/zoomable vertical diagram stage; full-screen mode (Esc exits); toolbar: −/+/Fit/Center/Validate</td><td class="mono">height, contentWidth/Height, validate, allowFullscreen, onBackgroundClick</td><td>FR-WFD-004, FR-GRAPH-005, NFR-RESP-006</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>WorkflowNode</b></td><td>Typed BPMN/DAG node (11 approved types); trace states green/amber/red; skipped = gray, non-interactive</td><td class="mono">type, name, x, y, status, selected, onSelect</td><td>ADR-010/016, FR-WFD-005</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>Edge</b></td><td>Directed edge; traversed black, default neutral, inactive gray dashed; branch labels</td><td class="mono">x1, y1, x2, y2, state, label</td><td>ADR-016</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>NodeInspector</b></td><td>Right panel: empty state, titled rows (mono for I/O), action slot (Go to Graph, Stop, Restart), collapsible</td><td class="mono">title, status, rows, actions, onClose</td><td>FR-WFD-003/008, FR-TRACE-011</td></tr>
</table>
<p><b>InfiniteList is built</b> (virtualized: windowed rows, load-more sentinel, 1,000-row cap). Named contracts still to implement from the approved inventory: <code>SearchInput, FilterBar, DateRangeFilter, SortControl, Chart, EmptyState, LoadingState, ErrorState, ConfirmationDialog, Drawer, Sheet, GraphNode</code> (GraphNode is currently WorkflowNode with <code>type="java"</code>; dialogs use the system <code>.dialog</code> classes).</p>

<h2>6. Design tokens</h2>
<h3>Theming pipeline</h3>
<table style="width:100%;font-size:9.5pt">
<tr>
<td style="background:#eef0fb;border:1.5pt solid #4a5ac9;text-align:center;padding:6pt;width:22%"><b>User picks</b><br>theme (System/Light/Dark)<br>accent (Indigo/Blue/Teal/Purple)</td>
<td style="border:none;text-align:center;color:#4a5ac9">▶</td>
<td style="background:#fff;border:1pt solid #9aa2d6;text-align:center;padding:6pt;width:24%"><b>Token remap on :root</b><br><span class="mono">ground/ink swap · ramps re-derive</span></td>
<td style="border:none;text-align:center;color:#4a5ac9">▶</td>
<td style="background:#fff;border:1pt solid #9aa2d6;text-align:center;padding:6pt;width:24%"><b>Everything re-themes</b><br>components read <span class="mono">var(--*)</span> only</td>
<td style="border:none;text-align:center;color:#4a5ac9">▶</td>
<td style="background:#f5f5f8;border:1pt solid #9aa2d6;text-align:center;padding:6pt;width:20%"><b>Persisted</b><br><span class="mono">localStorage</span></td>
</tr>
</table>
<p style="font-size:9pt;color:#5d5d60">Semantic status colors (success/warning/danger/inactive) stay fixed through every theme and accent (ADR-018).</p>
<table>
<tr><th>Group</th><th>Tokens</th><th>Usage</th></tr>
<tr><td>Color roles</td><td class="mono">--color-bg/-surface/-text/-accent/-divider + --color-neutral-100…900, --color-accent-100…900</td><td>Light steps for tints/hovers, 500 base, deep steps for text-on-tint and pressed states</td></tr>
<tr><td>Semantic status (fixed)</td><td class="mono">--color-success/-warning/-danger/-inactive (+ -100 tint, -800 text step each)</td><td>Success green, running/halted amber, failed red, inactive gray — stable across themes and accents</td></tr>
<tr><td>Type</td><td class="mono">--font-heading, --font-body, --font-mono</td><td>OS-shipped stacks only; mono carries rules, JSON, IDs, inputs/outputs</td></tr>
<tr><td>Layout</td><td class="mono">--layout-sidebar (232px), --layout-sidebar-collapsed (64px), --layout-topbar (56px), --layout-inspector (300px)</td><td>Shell dimensions</td></tr>
<tr><td>Space / radius / elevation</td><td class="mono">--space-1…8, --radius-sm/md/lg, --shadow-sm/md/lg</td><td>Square corners on cards/buttons per the Industry blueprint grammar</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>7. Interaction and color language</h2>
<ul>
<li>The accent (indigo #4a5ac9) is the interactive color: primary buttons, links, breadcrumbs, selection, focus (2px accent focus-visible ring), active nav (accent-700 label on accent-100 background).</li>
<li>Trends: color = business effect (green positive / red negative); the arrow only shows direction — lower duration is a green down-arrow.</li>
<li>Charts: single series accent blue; multi-series uses an accessible categorical palette with labels/legends.</li>
<li>Trace overlay: traversed edges black; non-traversed light gray; nodes green/amber/red with glyph + label; non-executed gray, dimmed and non-interactive.</li>
</ul>

<h2>8. Responsive behavior</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>Breakpoint</th><th>Shell</th><th>Content</th></tr>
<tr><td>Desktop</td><td>Full sidebar · top bar · inline inspector</td><td>4-column metrics; full tables</td></tr>
<tr><td>Tablet</td><td>Icon sidebar · inspector becomes overlay drawer</td><td>2-column metrics; filters into a drawer</td></tr>
<tr><td>Mobile</td><td>Top controls + nav drawer · inspector full-screen sheet</td><td>1-column metrics; essential table columns only, secondary data in row details; search collapses to a control</td></tr>
</table>
<p>BPMN/DAG canvases always stay scrollable and zoomable; nodes are never compressed to fit (NFR-RESP-006).</p>

<h2>9. Accessibility</h2>
<p>Target WCAG 2.2 AA: semantic HTML controls, keyboard operation with visible focus, status never by color alone (glyph + text everywhere), accessible names on icon-only controls, and interactive canvas nodes represented as real buttons in a navigable structure (NFR-A11Y-001…007).</p>

<h2>11. React implementation blueprint</h2>
<p>This section names the concrete React artifacts the build creates — components, hooks, routes, contexts and state transitions — so engineering estimates and PRs can reference them directly. Paths follow the handoff project (<code>templates/react-ts-handoff/</code>).</p>

<h3>11.1 Component tree</h3>
<table>
<tr><th>Path</th><th>Components created</th><th>Kind</th></tr>
<tr><td class="mono">src/app/</td><td>App · AppRoutes · ProtectedRoute</td><td>Composition roots</td></tr>
<tr><td class="mono">src/context/</td><td>UserProvider · TenantProvider · AppearanceProvider</td><td>Context providers</td></tr>
<tr><td class="mono">src/components/shell/</td><td>AppShell · Sidebar · TopBar · TenantToggle · GlobalSearch · ProfileMenu · Breadcrumbs · PageHeader</td><td>Shell primitives</td></tr>
<tr><td class="mono">src/components/data/</td><td>MetricCard · StatusIndicator · TrendIndicator · Badge · DataTable · <b>InfiniteList (virtualized — built)</b> · SearchInput · FilterBar · DateRangeFilter · EmptyState · LoadingState · ErrorState · ConfirmationDialog</td><td>Data/status primitives</td></tr>
<tr><td class="mono">src/components/canvas/</td><td>Canvas · WorkflowNode · GraphNode · Edge · NodeInspector</td><td>Canvas primitives</td></tr>
<tr><td class="mono">src/pages/</td><td>LoginPage · HomePage · WorkflowsPage · WorkflowDetailPage · GraphPage · RulesPage · RuleDetailPage · ExecutionsPage · TracePage · DeferredPage</td><td>Route modules (lazy)</td></tr>
</table>
<p>Rule: pages import primitives and hooks only — never fetch, never define visual styles (NFR-REACT-004).</p>

<h3>11.2 Hooks</h3>
<table>
<tr><th>Hook</th><th>Signature (conceptual)</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
<tr><td class="mono">useUser()</td><td class="mono">→ { user, roles, permissions, can(action) }</td><td>Identity + permission checks; <code>can('workflow.create')</code> gates the + Workflow button</td></tr>
<tr><td class="mono">useTenant()</td><td class="mono">→ { tenant, tenants, setTenant }</td><td>Tenant context; switching invalidates every tenant-scoped query (FR-SHELL-005)</td></tr>
<tr><td class="mono">useAppearance()</td><td class="mono">→ { theme, accent, setTheme, setAccent }</td><td>Token remap on :root + localStorage persistence (NFR-REACT-005)</td></tr>
<tr><td class="mono">useWorkflows(filters)</td><td class="mono">→ { data, isLoading, error, fetchNextPage }</td><td>Workflow inventory, paged for infinite scroll</td></tr>
<tr><td class="mono">useWorkflow(id) / useRule(id)</td><td class="mono">→ { data, isLoading, error }</td><td>Detail records incl. BPMN definition / rule definition</td></tr>
<tr><td class="mono">useExecutions(filters)</td><td class="mono">→ { data, …, fetchNextPage }</td><td>Executions; filter change resets pages and scroll position</td></tr>
<tr><td class="mono">useExecutionTrace(id)</td><td class="mono">→ { execution, workflowVersion, path }</td><td>Historical workflow version + traversed path (FR-TRACE-002)</td></tr>
<tr><td class="mono">useExecutionActions(id)</td><td class="mono">→ { stop, restartFrom(nodeId) }</td><td>Mutations with confirmation; restart returns linked new execution id</td></tr>
<tr><td class="mono">useGlobalSearch(query)</td><td class="mono">→ { results, isLoading }</td><td>Debounced, tenant-scoped search across workflows/rules/executions</td></tr>
<tr><td class="mono">useCanvasViewport()</td><td class="mono">→ { zoom, setZoom, fit, center, fullscreen }</td><td>Canvas view state, local to each canvas instance</td></tr>
<tr><td class="mono">useInfiniteScroll(ref, cb)</td><td class="mono">→ void</td><td>IntersectionObserver trigger for InfiniteList</td></tr>
</table>
<p>Data hooks wrap a query layer (TanStack Query recommended: caching, invalidation, retries). Today they resolve from <code>fixtures.ts</code> adapters; swapping in real APIs changes only the adapter (FR-MOCK-003).</p>

<h3>11.3 Routes (React Router v6, all lazy)</h3>
<table>
<tr><th>Path</th><th>Element</th><th>Guard / loader notes</th></tr>
<tr><td class="mono">/login</td><td class="mono">&lt;LoginPage /&gt;</td><td>Redirects to /home when already authenticated</td></tr>
<tr><td class="mono">/ (layout route)</td><td class="mono">&lt;ProtectedRoute&gt;&lt;AppShell /&gt;&lt;/ProtectedRoute&gt;</td><td>Shell renders once; children swap in &lt;Outlet /&gt;</td></tr>
<tr><td class="mono">/home</td><td class="mono">&lt;HomePage /&gt;</td><td>index redirect from /</td></tr>
<tr><td class="mono">/workflows</td><td class="mono">&lt;WorkflowsPage /&gt;</td><td>Search/filter state in URL search params</td></tr>
<tr><td class="mono">/workflows/:workflowId</td><td class="mono">&lt;WorkflowDetailPage /&gt;</td><td>Selected node id in search param <code>?node=</code> (deep-linkable)</td></tr>
<tr><td class="mono">/workflows/:workflowId/graphs/:graphId</td><td class="mono">&lt;GraphPage /&gt;</td><td>Breadcrumbs derive from params</td></tr>
<tr><td class="mono">/rules · /rules/:ruleId</td><td class="mono">&lt;RulesPage /&gt; · &lt;RuleDetailPage /&gt;</td><td></td></tr>
<tr><td class="mono">/executions</td><td class="mono">&lt;ExecutionsPage /&gt;</td><td>Filters in URL search params; shareable views</td></tr>
<tr><td class="mono">/executions/:executionId</td><td class="mono">&lt;TracePage /&gt;</td><td><code>?node=</code> selects the inspected node</td></tr>
<tr><td class="mono">/monitoring · /docs · /examples</td><td class="mono">&lt;DeferredPage /&gt;</td><td>Visible-but-deferred (FR-SHELL-010)</td></tr>
<tr><td class="mono">*</td><td class="mono">&lt;ErrorState kind="not-found" /&gt;</td><td></td></tr>
</table>

<h3>11.4 State — what lives where, and what changes it</h3>
<table>
<tr><th>State</th><th>Lives in</th><th>Changed by → effect</th></tr>
<tr><td>Session (user, roles, permissions)</td><td class="mono">UserProvider</td><td>SSO callback → shell renders; logout → redirect /login, caches cleared</td></tr>
<tr><td>Tenant</td><td class="mono">TenantProvider</td><td>TenantToggle pick → all tenant-scoped queries invalidated; current route re-fetches; search rescopes</td></tr>
<tr><td>Theme + accent</td><td class="mono">AppearanceProvider</td><td>ProfileMenu pick → tokens remapped on :root, persisted; no component re-render needed beyond the menu</td></tr>
<tr><td>Server data (workflows, rules, executions, traces)</td><td class="mono">Query cache</td><td>Route mount / filter change / tenant change → fetch; Stop/Restart mutation → invalidate execution + list</td></tr>
<tr><td>URL state (filters, search text, selected node)</td><td class="mono">Router search params</td><td>User input → URL updates → deep-linkable, survives refresh, back button works</td></tr>
<tr><td>Sidebar collapsed</td><td class="mono">AppShell local + localStorage</td><td>Collapse click → width token flips</td></tr>
<tr><td>Canvas viewport (zoom, fullscreen)</td><td class="mono">useCanvasViewport (local)</td><td>Toolbar → transform updates; Esc exits fullscreen; never global</td></tr>
<tr><td>Dialog open/confirm</td><td class="mono">Page local state</td><td>Action click → open; Confirm → mutation → close + toast</td></tr>
</table>
<p>Deliberate choice: no Redux/Zustand at baseline. Server cache + contexts + URL params cover the approved scope; a global store is added only if a future feature demonstrates the need.</p>

<h3>11.5 Key state flows (sequences)</h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Tenant switch:</b> TenantToggle → <code>setTenant</code> → provider updates → query keys (all include tenant) go stale → active page shows LoadingState → fresh tenant data renders. Search box clears.</li>
<li><b>Node inspection:</b> node click → <code>setSearchParams({node: id})</code> → NodeInspector reads the param → renders config/execution rows; background click removes the param → inspector empty state.</li>
<li><b>Restart from node:</b> inspector Restart → ConfirmationDialog → <code>restartFrom(nodeId)</code> mutation → optimistic “running” badge → on success navigate to the NEW execution id (linked to the old one) → trace re-renders.</li>
<li><b>Infinite scroll:</b> sentinel zone triggers <code>fetchNextPage</code> → rows append into the <b>virtualized</b> InfiniteList — only the visible window (~15 rows + overscan) exists in the DOM at any scroll depth; a 1,000-row cap shows “refine your filters” instead of loading forever; changing any filter resets pagination and scrolls to top (FR-EXEC-007).</li>
</ul>

<h3>11.6 Additional React concerns</h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Code splitting:</b> every page module behind <code>React.lazy</code> + a route-level <code>&lt;Suspense fallback=&lt;LoadingState/&gt;&gt;</code> (NFR-REACT-006); the canvas bundle splits separately — it loads only for BPMN/graph/trace routes.</li>
<li><b>Error boundaries:</b> one per route module rendering <code>ErrorState</code>; shell stays alive when a page crashes.</li>
<li><b>Memoization:</b> node/edge arrays and DataTable rows are memoized; canvas re-renders on viewport change must not re-create node components (React.memo on WorkflowNode/Edge).</li>
<li><b>Accessibility hooks:</b> focus trap in dialogs and the fullscreen canvas; focus returns to the invoking control on close; canvas nodes are real &lt;button&gt;s in DOM order.</li>
<li><b>Testing seams:</b> primitives get RTL component tests against their .d.ts contracts; pages get interaction tests with mocked hooks; the fixtures layer doubles as MSW seed data later.</li>
<li><b>Definition of done for a primitive:</b> typed props matching the contract · tokens only · keyboard + focus states · empty/loading/error variants where applicable · RTL tests · a specimen card.</li>
</ul>

<h2>13. Capability module structure</h2>
<p>The UI is one repository whose routes are partitioned into capability packages, so a deployment can be built containing only the capabilities it is entitled to (ADR-033/035). Capability is decided at build time; tenant identity is applied at deploy time. Those two must never swap places.</p>

<h3>13.1 Folder structure</h3>
<pre class="tree">visualization-ui/
  packages/
    core/                       # always shipped — the only package that knows about "the app"
      src/app/                  # App · AppRoutes · ProtectedRoute · CapabilityGate
      src/shell/                # AppShell · Sidebar · TopBar · Breadcrumbs · PageHeader
      src/primitives/           # the 14 design-system components (§5)
      src/context/              # UserProvider · TenantProvider · AppearanceProvider
                                #   · CapabilityProvider
      src/registry/             # RouteRegistry · NavRegistry — capabilities register INTO these
      src/query/                # query client, cache policy, error normalisation
      src/styles/styles.css     # the token stylesheet
                                # core MUST NOT import from any capability package
    capability-monitor/         # executions, trace, alerts, monitoring overview,
                                #   read-only workflow + graph views
    capability-build/           # workflow authoring, rules, validate, publish
    capability-tasks/           # task inventory and task detail (in design — §13.4)
    capability-docs/            # documentation surfaces
    capability-operate/         # stop / restart / intervene actions inside trace
  apps/
    app-monitor/  app-build/  app-tasks/  app-docs/  app-full/
                                # composition roots — imports and a Vite config, no UI code
  tenants/
    &lt;tenant&gt;/deployment.json    # bundle, domain, region, idp — written by onboarding
    &lt;tenant&gt;/branding.json      # accent token, product name, logo asset ref
    &lt;tenant&gt;/overrides.json     # labels, column defaults, in-capability toggles
    &lt;tenant&gt;/infra/             # CDK parameters for their account
  ds-base/                      # design-system loader shared by all apps</pre>
<p>A capability package owns its routes, its pages, its hooks and its API client. It may import from <code>core</code>; it may not import from another capability package. Cross-capability needs are expressed as a contribution to a core registry, never as a direct dependency — which is what lets any subset compile.</p>

<h3>13.2 How a capability registers</h3>
<p>Each package exports one manifest. The composition root imports the manifests it wants; nothing else in the app enumerates capabilities.</p>
<pre class="tree">// packages/capability-monitor/src/manifest.ts
export const monitorCapability: CapabilityManifest = {
  id: 'monitor',
  nav: [{ group: 'Monitor', items: [
    { to: '/executions', label: 'Executions', icon: 'activity' },
    { to: '/alerts',     label: 'Alerts',     icon: 'bell', badge: 'alertCount' },
  ]}],
  routes: [
    { path: '/executions',     element: lazy(() =&gt; import('./pages/ExecutionsPage')) },
    { path: '/executions/:id', element: lazy(() =&gt; import('./pages/TracePage')) },
    { path: '/alerts',         element: lazy(() =&gt; import('./pages/AlertsPage')) },
  ],
  landing: '/executions',      // candidate landing route, priority-ordered in core
};

// apps/app-monitor/src/main.tsx — the ENTIRE difference between bundles
bootstrap([coreCapability, monitorCapability, operateCapability]);</pre>
<p>Three consequences follow, and they are the point of the design. The bundler tree-shakes every capability not imported by the composition root, so authoring code is <b>absent from the build output</b>, not merely lazy (ADR-038). Core contains no list of capability ids, so reading <code>core</code> discloses nothing about what else exists. And nav, routes and landing route all derive from the same manifests, so they cannot drift out of step.</p>

<h3>13.3 CapabilityGate — and what it is not</h3>
<p><code>useCapability('build')</code> answers whether a capability is present in <i>this</i> build, and <code>&lt;CapabilityGate cap="build"&gt;</code> renders children only if it is. Its legitimate use is <b>cross-capability links</b>: a trace page in the full bundle links to the workflow editor, and in a monitoring bundle renders the workflow name as text. It is not an authorization mechanism and not a way to hide routes — an absent capability has no route to hide, and permission checks remain <code>useUser().can(action)</code> as before. Two orthogonal questions: capability asks "is this feature in this deployment", permission asks "may this person use it".</p>

<h3>13.4 Tasks (in design)</h3>
<p>Tasks is a first-class capability package within the Experience UI, not a section of another capability. It is scaffolded now — package, manifest, nav group, inventory route and detail route — against the Inventory page pattern, so the shape is fixed while the content is being designed. It ships in the <code>tasks</code> and <code>full</code> bundles only; the monitoring bundle does not contain it. Nothing else in the codebase changes when its design lands, which is the test that the module boundary is correct.</p>

<h2>14. Browser memory and component interaction</h2>
<p>This section is the part of the architecture that keeps a long-lived internal tool from degrading over a working day: what is allowed to accumulate in the tab, what evicts it, and how components exchange state without re-rendering each other unnecessarily.</p>

<h3>14.1 The four memory pools</h3>
<table>
<tr><th>Pool</th><th>Holds</th><th>Bound</th><th>Evicted by</th></tr>
<tr><td><b>DOM</b></td><td>Rendered nodes</td><td>Constant — visible window + overscan (~30 rows; canvas: viewport tiles)</td><td>Virtualization; nothing off-screen exists</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>Query cache</b></td><td>Server payloads keyed by query</td><td>5-minute stale, 15-minute GC; inventories keep a ~500-row window of pages</td><td>Age, tenant switch (full clear), mutation invalidation, page-window trimming</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>Diagram store</b></td><td>Parsed nodes/edges per (workflow, version), plus loaded tile ids</td><td>Two diagrams; tiles beyond 2× viewport dropped</td><td>LRU on navigation away from a canvas; cleared on version change</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>Component state</b></td><td>Zoom, selection, dialog, sidebar</td><td>Trivial — scalars</td><td>Unmount; nothing persists except sidebar collapse (localStorage)</td></tr>
</table>
<p>The invariant behind all four: <b>memory is a function of what is on screen, not of how long the tab has been open or how deep the user has scrolled.</b> Anything that violates that is a defect, not a tuning opportunity.</p>

<h3>14.2 Virtualized inventory — memory over a long scroll</h3>
<div class="seq">scroll depth →      0 rows        200 rows       800 rows       1,000 rows (cap)
                    │              │              │              │
DOM rows            30             30             30             30        ← constant
cached pages        1              4              10             10        ← window trims oldest
detached listeners  0              0              0              0         ← observers unbind on unmount
                    │              │              │              │
                    │              │              │              └─ cap notice replaces sentinel:
                    │              │              │                 "1,000 rows loaded — narrow your filter"
                    │              │              └─ pages older than the window are dropped;
                    │              │                 scrolling back re-fetches from cursor
                    │              └─ sentinel enters viewport → fetchNextPage(cursor)
                    └─ first page + skeleton

filter change → pages reset to 1, scroll to top, cursor discarded, in-flight request aborted</div>
<p class="cap">Figure A — The list is bounded in three independent ways: DOM by windowing, cache by page trimming, and total load by the 1,000-row cap. A filter change is a reset, never a merge.</p>

<h3>14.3 Canvas viewport and tile lifecycle</h3>
<div class="seq">                    ┌──────────────────────────────────┐
 stage (logical) ──▶│  tiles: [2,1] [3,1] [2,2] [3,2]   │  loaded = viewport × 2
                    │  ┌─────────────┐                 │
                    │  │  viewport   │  ◀─ CSS transform: translate + scale
                    │  │  (visible)  │     zoom and pan cost ZERO requests
                    │  └─────────────┘     and ZERO re-renders of node components
                    └──────────────────────────────────┘

pan crosses tile boundary → request bbox tile → append nodes/edges to diagram store
                          → drop tiles outside 2× viewport (LRU)
zoom &lt; 60%                → hide labels, keep shapes + status (no data change)
nodes &gt; ~2,000            → BFF returns lod:"summary"; detail arrives on zoom-in
navigate away             → diagram store keeps 2 most-recent (workflow, version) entries
version changes           → entry invalidated — the key is immutable, so this is a new key</div>
<p class="cap">Figure B — Zoom and pan are presentation-only. Only crossing into unloaded space is a network event, which is why a 4,000-node diagram stays interactive.</p>

<h3>14.4 Component interaction — shell, page, canvas, inspector</h3>
<div class="seq">  AppShell (never remounts on navigation)
     │  context: user · tenant · appearance · capabilities
     │
     ├─ Sidebar ───── nav click ──▶ router.navigate(path)
     ├─ TopBar ───── tenant switch ─▶ TenantProvider.set() ─▶ queryClient.clear()
     │                                                          └▶ current route refetches
     │              appearance ────▶ tokens remapped on :root  (NO React re-render)
     │
     └─ &lt;Outlet /&gt; ─▶ Page (lazy, own error boundary)
           │
           ├─ PageHeader   ← props only
           ├─ FilterBar ─── change ─▶ setSearchParams()  ─▶ URL is the single source of truth
           │                                              └▶ query key changes → refetch
           └─ Canvas (memoised on { nodes, edges })
                 │  local: zoom, pan, fullscreen  — never lifted, never in context
                 ├─ WorkflowNode×N (memoised per node id)
                 │     └─ click ─▶ setSearchParams({ node: id })   ← selection lives in the URL
                 └─ NodeInspector
                       └─ reads ?node= ─▶ useNode(id) ─▶ lazy I/O fetch on expand

Re-render containment:
  zoom change      → one CSS transform on the stage element; no node re-renders
  node selection   → previously + newly selected node only; siblings memoised by id
  theme change     → zero React renders; CSS custom properties do the work
  tenant change    → full data refetch, shell intact, scroll position reset</div>
<p class="cap">Figure C — State flows down through props and context; changes flow up through the router. The URL carries anything a user might bookmark, share or reach with the Back button — filters, search text and selected node — which also keeps it out of component state.</p>

<h3>14.5 Leak rules</h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Every subscription unbinds on unmount</b> — IntersectionObserver, ResizeObserver, <code>window</code> listeners, timers. The canvas registers pointer listeners on the stage element, never on <code>document</code>, so a route change cannot orphan them.</li>
<li><b>In-flight requests abort</b> on unmount and on filter change (AbortController through the query layer), so a fast-typing user cannot stack ten pending searches.</li>
<li><b>No unbounded arrays in state.</b> Anything that grows with user activity — loaded pages, tiles, toasts, recent searches — has an explicit cap written next to its declaration.</li>
<li><b>Detached DOM is a bug.</b> Node references held after unmount (a cached ref in a closure, a memo keyed on an element) retain their subtree; refs are cleared in cleanup.</li>
<li><b>Long-session budget:</b> a tab left open for an eight-hour shift, navigating freely, must stay under ~250 MB heap. Verified by a scripted soak — navigate, scroll to cap, open three traces, switch tenant, repeat — comparing heap after forced GC at start and end.</li>
</ul>

<h3>14.6 Performance budgets</h3>
<table>
<tr><th>Interaction</th><th>Budget</th><th>Mechanism</th></tr>
<tr><td>Route change (chunk cached)</td><td>&lt; 150 ms to first paint</td><td>Lazy chunk + skeleton; shell never remounts</td></tr>
<tr><td>Scroll at any depth</td><td>60 fps</td><td>Constant DOM window; no per-row layout thrash</td></tr>
<tr><td>Canvas zoom / pan</td><td>60 fps</td><td>Single composited transform; no React render</td></tr>
<tr><td>Node select → inspector</td><td>&lt; 100 ms</td><td>Data already in the diagram store; I/O bodies load after</td></tr>
<tr><td>Filter change → first rows</td><td>&lt; 400 ms</td><td>Abort previous, reset pages, single cursor request</td></tr>
<tr><td>Initial load (warm cache)</td><td>&lt; 1.5 s to interactive</td><td>Hashed immutable assets; capability chunks only</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>15. Deliverables map</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>Path</th><th>What it is</th></tr>
<tr><td class="mono">styles.css</td><td>Token sheet + component classes (the one stylesheet)</td></tr>
<tr><td class="mono">components/platform-shell/ · platform-data/ · platform-canvas/</td><td>React primitives (.jsx) + typed contracts (.d.ts) + live demo pages</td></tr>
<tr><td class="mono">templates/platform-app/</td><td>Interactive application: app.jsx, pages-build.jsx, pages-monitor.jsx, fixtures.js</td></tr>
<tr><td class="mono">templates/react-ts-handoff/</td><td>Standalone React + TypeScript Vite project (components, pages, fixtures, README)</td></tr>
<tr><td class="mono">vanilla/industry-shell.js</td><td>Framework-free custom elements (shell layer) + window.IndustryTheme token remap</td></tr>
<tr><td class="mono">exports/Platform Wireframes.html</td><td>Self-contained interactive wireframes for stakeholder review</td></tr>
<tr><td class="mono">UI Architecture.html</td><td>This architecture as a visual blueprint diagram</td></tr>
<tr><td class="mono">readme.md · theme.json</td><td>Usage guide and machine-readable theme record</td></tr>
</table>

